The member copies here (a pointer, an index, a type and a flag) are trivial and already in the initializer list. Any real cost is in copying `FieldBase`, which this function can't change without altering behavior. So the rewrite keeps the same semantics and stays in the initializer-list form, which is already optimal. Don't expect a measurable speedup from this change alone.

```cpp
Field::Field(const Field &field)
    : FieldBase(field),
      profile(field.profile),
      profileIndex(field.profileIndex),
      type(field.type),
      isFieldExpanded(field.isFieldExpanded)
{
}
```